{"id": "EUVD-2026-103930", "enisaUuid": "9349b471-0c3e-3a83-9ca9-ecc15d32fb20", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\niio: adc: ade9000: fix NULL pointer dereference in clkout registration\n\nade9000_setup_clkout() passes NULL as the register address when\nregistering a divider clock. During clock registration, the common\nclock framework calls clk_divider_recalc_rate(), which dereferences\nthe address through readl(). As a result, probing an ADE9000 configured\nas a clock provider with an external input clock crashes.\n\nCLKOUT passes CLKIN through without changing its rate. Register it as\na 1:1 fixed-factor clock, which does not require register access.\n\nThis change does not affect the configuration using the internal clock,\nfor which the driver does not register a clock provider.", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T15:45:31", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:23:45", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d2400175228fbc10b29c49a7b5f70a7e80d144dd", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/134aa31a8d4e71f6ab1d155ad7b4502508832f72", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/49ee1c6a3ebda6b7de06b2961b0e09c1c3fe536a"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-98676", "GHSA-qchf-h949-mmvh"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.2, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "296a14a5-17bf-38b3-b12b-7e6729e2892b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.18"}, {"id": "6930aec6-97d1-3f58-b019-37a5164f513b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "81de7b4619fc3682a3bedaa7e8d6b2d67ab4e10a <49ee1c6a3ebda6b7de06b2961b0e09c1c3fe536a"}, {"id": "7cb40bc6-01e9-3114-9906-43e82f815f50", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "81215c4c-ec0c-37b4-a152-a876b2be6e4f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "81de7b4619fc3682a3bedaa7e8d6b2d67ab4e10a <134aa31a8d4e71f6ab1d155ad7b4502508832f72"}, {"id": "